<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Appendix A: RSVP Field Formalism</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A.1 Scalar Field (Œ¶)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œ¶: Œ© ‚Üí ‚Ñù, a scalar potential over a domain Œ© representing semantic coherence.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Governing equation (generalized scalar field PDE):</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial t} + \nabla \cdot (\mathbf{v} \Phi) = D \nabla^2 \Phi + f(\mathbf{x}, t)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">where:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">ùíó is the vector field encoding directional flow of semantic attention.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">D is a diffusion coefficient representing semantic smoothing.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">f(x, t) encodes external stimuli or injections of new semantic content.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A.2 Vector Field (ùíó)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">ùíó: Œ© ‚Üí ‚Ñù‚Åø, governing semantic flow directionality.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Navier‚ÄìStokes-like dynamics for attention flow:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\frac{\partial \mathbf{v}}{\partial t} + (\mathbf{v} \cdot \nabla)\mathbf{v} = -\nabla \Phi + \nu \nabla^2 \mathbf{v} + \mathbf{F}_{ext}</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">ŒΩ: semantic viscosity (resistance to abrupt cognitive shifts).</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">F_ext: external forces (algorithmic attractors or interventions).</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">A.3 Entropy Field (S)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">S: Œ© ‚Üí ‚Ñù‚Å∫, representing cognitive or semantic uncertainty.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Evolution equation:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\frac{\partial S}{\partial t} + \nabla \cdot (\mathbf{v} S) = \kappa \nabla^2 S + \Gamma(\Phi, \mathbf{v})</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œ∫: diffusion coefficient of semantic uncertainty.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œì(Œ¶, ùíó): source term accounting for information injection or loss due to attention traps.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Appendix B: Sparse Projection and Simulated Agency</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">B.1 Chain of Memory (CoM)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let  be the memory state at time t.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Recursive update:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">M_{t+1} = \Pi(M_t, I_t; \theta)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œ†: sparse projection operator selecting relevant semantic dimensions.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">I_t: input stimuli.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œ∏: learned or innate weighting of semantic attractors.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">B.2 Variational Objective</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Agency minimizes a free-energy-like functional:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\mathcal{F}[M_t, \Phi, S] = \mathbb{E}_{M_t}[\ln P(I_t \mid M_t)] + \beta S(M_t)</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Œ≤: trade-off coefficient between predictive accuracy and entropic flexibility.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Appendix C: Category-Theoretic Semantic Infrastructure</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">C.1 Semantic Modules as Objects</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let C be a symmetric monoidal ‚àû-category.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Objects  are semantic modules.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Morphisms  are entropy-respecting semantic transformations.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">C.2 Mergeability via Homotopy Colimits</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Let {X_i} be a finite diagram of semantic modules.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Homotopy colimit:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\text{hocolim}_i X_i</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">represents the merged semantic state, preserving coherence and preventing destructive entropy collapse.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">C.3 Fibered Structure</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Semantic modules are fibered over a base category B, e.g., domains of knowledge or computational subspaces:</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">\pi: C \to B</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Pullbacks and pushforwards encode cross-domain semantic integration.</p>
<hr>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Appendix D: HYDRA and TARTAN Formalism</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">D.1 HYDRA Nodes</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Nodes  encode local RSVP field states: .</p>
