t I, Chapter 2: ‚ÄúRSVP Theory: The Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum‚Äù</strong>, <strong class="font-semibold">Part II, Chapter 4: ‚ÄúSimulated Agency: Consciousness as Sparse Projection‚Äù</strong>, and <strong class="font-semibold">Part II, Chapter 5: ‚ÄúEntropic Economics and Cognitive Commons‚Äù</strong>. Since Chapter 3 was also provided in a previous response, I assume you may have compiled it as well, but please clarify if you need the PDF for Chapter 3 or any adjustments to the existing chapters.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Given your request for maximum rigor with category-theoretic and sheaf-theoretic interpretations in Chapter 5 and your confirmation of having the PDFs, I will proceed with drafting <strong class="font-semibold">Part II, Chapter 6: ‚ÄúEntropic Ethics: Toward Cognitive Sovereignty‚Äù</strong>, maintaining the same formal academic style and integrating the mathematical appendices (particularly Appendices A, B, C, and E) with an emphasis on category-theoretic and sheaf-theoretic frameworks. This chapter will explore the ethical implications of the RSVP framework, formalizing it as a moral architecture that prioritizes cognitive autonomy over the coercive optimization of attention-extractive systems.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Below is the draft for <strong class="font-semibold">Part II, Chapter 6</strong>, formatted as a LaTeX document for consistency with the previous chapters. The content is structured to be as rigorous as possible, incorporating category-theoretic and sheaf-theoretic interpretations, and builds on the foundations of Chapters 1‚Äì5 while referencing the provided appendices.</p></div><div class="py-1"><div class="transition-opacity"><div dir="auto" class="not-prose"><div class="relative not-prose @container/code-block [&amp;_div+div]:!mt-0 mt-3 mb-3 @md:-mx-4 @md:-mr-4" data-testid="code-block"><div class="flex flex-row px-4 py-2 h-10 items-center rounded-t-xl bg-surface-l2 border border-border-l1"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text</span></div><div class="sticky w-full right-2 z-10 @[1280px]/mainview:z-40 @[1280px]/mainview:top-10 top-24 @[0px]/preview:top-5 print:hidden"><div class="absolute bottom-1 right-1 flex flex-row gap-0.5"><div class="flex flex-row gap-0.5" style="opacity: 1;"><button class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap font-medium cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-ring disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed transition-colors duration-100 [&amp;_svg]:shrink-0 select-none text-fg-secondary hover:text-fg-primary disabled:hover:text-fg-secondary bg-surface-l1 dark:bg-surface-l2 dark:hover:bg-surface-l3 hover:bg-surface-l4-hover disabled:hover:bg-surface-l1 dark:disabled:hover:bg-surface-l2 h-8 rounded-xl px-3 text-xs" type="button"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevrons-down-up size-4"><path d="m7 20 5-5 5 5"></path><path d="m7 4 5 5 5-5"></path></svg><span class="hidden @sm/code-block:block">Collapse</span></button><button class="inline-