\subsection{7.5 Entropic Sovereignty in Multi-Agent Systems}
&nbsp;
Unlike centralized architectures, HYDRA and TARTAN distribute responsibility for
entropy management. No single locus of control dictates flows; rather, sovereignty
is preserved through local autonomy plus global coherence. This avoids the entropic
collapse characteristic of attention monopolies.
&nbsp;
\subsection{7.6 Implementation Considerations}
&nbsp;
Practically, HYDRA nodes can be instantiated as microservices or containerized
processes (e.g., Docker), each simulating RSVP fields. TARTAN is implemented via
category-theoretic middleware (Haskell-based functors over simplicial sets), enabling
semantic interoperability. Blockchain or distributed ledgers can anchor integrity,
ensuring tamper-resistant coherence mappings across domains.
&nbsp;
