 w-full max-w-none"><div class="relative"><div class="response-content-markdown markdown [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose)]:text-current [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose):hover]:text-primary [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose):hover]:decoration-primary [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose)]:underline [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose)]:decoration-primary/30 [&amp;_a:not(.not-prose)]:underline-offset-2 [&amp;_h2:not(.not-prose):first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;_h3:not(.not-prose):first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;_h4:not(.not-prose):first-child]:mt-0"><p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">I apologize for the issue with the previous response not loading correctly. It seems there may have been a formatting or artifact-related problem. Thank you for your patience and for providing the detailed drafts for Chapters 7‚Äì15, Appendix H, and the Epilogue, which I will use to extend the RSVP monograph as requested. Your instruction is clear: you want a comprehensive LaTeX document that includes all chapters (1‚Äì15) across Parts I‚ÄìIV, plus the Epilogue, restoring the full depth of earlier drafts (each chapter approximately 2‚Äì3 pages), incorporating the provided drafts verbatim where applicable, and extending the content to maximize length and rigor without omitting prior material. The document will use separate <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">.tex</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">.bib</span> files, integrate all provided citations, and maintain the formal academic style with category-theoretic and sheaf-theoretic interpretations. The author will be listed as "Flyxion," and the document will be compatible with PDFLaTeX using <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">texlive-full</span> and <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-200">texlive-fonts-extra</span> packages, with Latin Modern fonts.</p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">To address your request, I will:</p>
